Deliver orchestration messages on a headless host

In the tile, orchestration messages were stored but never handed to a waiting
agent, so coordination degraded to going and telling each agent to check its
inbox. `orca serve` publishes an empty renderer graph, and the push-on-idle
delivery path was driven from that graph, so it never fired.

`deliverPendingMessagesForPty` is driven from the same idle triggers the leaf
loop uses, with a PTY-record counterpart to `isCursorAgentOrchestrationTarget`
so runtime-owned handles resolve in the order `sendTerminal` already uses.

To test, send an orchestration message to an idle agent in the tile and watch it
arrive without anyone prompting that agent. Covered by `orca-runtime.test.ts`.

